只输出严格JSON，恰好包含id（metadata.id原样）、summary_zh（15到140个Unicode字符，通常40到100字）、category（枚举）、tags（2到5个不重复关键词，每个最多30字符）、confidence（0到1，仅自评）、insufficient_evidence（布尔）、evidence（1到3个对象，每个恰好包含paragraph_id、fact）、limitations（0到5个字符串）。只选择输入中长度20至120字符的完整片段编号；fact是该片段支持的中文事实转述。不要输出quote，不要自行抄写、拼接、删改或补造引用。程序会按编号附上原文。一个编号只用一次；最多3条证据。不得增加字段。
摘要和limitations保留会改变功能意义的前提、平台例外和限制：设密码后才认证、页面保持打开才提醒、依赖外部组件、估算不等于保证。只写已实现功能，不将规划当完成。证据不足就标记，不编造。
图像识别/分类不是媒体创作，没有贴切类别归other；量化、计算与领域研究归search-research，不因多智能体实现归agents-automation；模型/CLI适配与插件开发工具归coding-development；市场/精选目录按搜索发现归search-research。不要按附属同步、备份或评论功能分类。不要推断本机客户端等于本地模型。
摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Structured safe Git tools for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): git_status/diff/log/branch/stage/commit/stash/show + destructive-command guard","id":"gh:1333375305","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-tool-git","slug":"lxj808624/dsh-tool-git","topics":["deepseek-harness","dsh-plugin","git","tool"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Structured safe Git tools for DeepSeek Harness (dsh): git_status/diff/log/branch/stage/commit/stash/"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"show + destructive-command guard"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-tool-git"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Structured, safe Git tool family for DeepSeek Harness (`dsh`)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Coding agents reach for git constantly, but the stock runtime only offers raw `bash`.\n`dsh-tool-git`"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" gives the model eight structured tools that run `git` through a\nshell-free subprocess runner and re"},{"id":"p4s3","text":"turn canonical JSON values — plus a\n`tools/pre-execute` safety gate that stops destructive git opera"},{"id":"p4s4","text":"tions\n(force push, hard reset, rebase, amend, branch deletion, …) before they happen,\nwhether the mo"},{"id":"p4s5","text":"del calls them through these tools **or** through a shell tool."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"- **No shell injection**: every command goes through `execFile` with an explicit\nargument array. Mod"},{"id":"p5s2","text":"el-supplied paths and messages are never string-interpolated.\n- **Machine output**: porcelain v2, `-"},{"id":"p5s3","text":"-numstat`, and `--format` records are parsed\ninto structured JSON, not prose.\n- **Safety by default*"},{"id":"p5s4","text":"*: destructive operations are denied with an explanation\nunless you opt into `ask` (approval prompt)"},{"id":"p5s5","text":"ve operations are denied with an explanation\nunless you opt into `ask` (approval prompt) or `allow`."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Tools"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"| Tool | What it does |"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"| `git_status` | Working tree state: branch, ahead/behind, staged / unstaged / untracked files |\n| `"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"git_diff` | Per-file insertion/deletion stats, optional unified patch, `--cached` / `rev` bases |\n| "},{"id":"p8s3","text":"`git_log` | Commit history: hash, author, date, subject, body; `maxCount`, `rev` range, `path` filte"},{"id":"p8s4","text":"r |\n| `git_branch` | Branches with upstream and ahead/behind tracking state |\n| `git_stage` | Stage "},{"id":"p8s5","text":"explicit paths, or all / tracked-only changes |\n| `git_commit` | Create a commit with a message; ret"},{"id":"p8s6","text":"urns hash and statistics |\n| `git_stash` | `list` / `push` / `pop` stashes, with conflict-safe pop |"},{"id":"p8s7","text":"\n| `git_show` | One commit: metadata, per-file stats, optional patch |\n| `git_fetch` | Download refs"},{"id":"p8s8","text":" from a remote without touching the worktree |\n| `git_pull` | Fast-forward-only by default; reports "},{"id":"p8s9","text":"`not-fast-forward` / `conflict` outcomes |\n| `git_remote` | List configured remotes with fetch/push "},{"id":"p8s10","text":"URLs |\n| `git_checkout` | Switch branches, or create and switch (`-b`); never discards changes |"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Every tool accepts an optional `repoDir` argument and reports the resolved\nrepository root in its re"},{"id":"p9s2","text":" tool accepts an optional `repoDir` argument and reports the resolved\nrepository root in its result."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Safety gate"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"The gate listens on `tools/pre-execute` and inspects every tool call:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"- **The plugin's own tools** — e.g. `git_commit` with `amend: true`.\n- **Shell tools** — `bash`, `to"},{"id":"p12s2","text":"ol:bash`, `bash_persistent`, `terminal`,\n`tool:terminal`, `pwsh` — scanning their command text for d"},{"id":"p12s3","text":"estructive git\ninvocations such as:"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"`push --force` / `--force-with-lease` · `push --delete` · `reset --hard` ·\n`clean -f` · `branch -d/-"},{"id":"p13s2","text":"D` · `tag -d` · `rebase` · `pull --rebase` ·\n`commit --amend` · `checkout --` / `checkout .` / `chec"},{"id":"p13s3","text":"kout -f` ·\n`switch -f` · `restore` (discarding worktree) · `rm -r` ·\n`update-ref -d` · `filter-branc"},{"id":"p13s4","text":"ut -f` ·\n`switch -f` · `restore` (discarding worktree) · `rm -r` ·\n`update-ref -d` · `filter-branch`"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"Pattern matching is per-command: it never crosses `|`, `;`, or newline\nboundaries, so `git add . && "},{"id":"p14s2","text":"git push --force` is still caught but innocent\ncompound commands are not misread."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"**This is a policy guardrail, not a sandbox.** An agent that can run arbitrary\ncode can always route"},{"id":"p15s2","text":" around a string matcher (aliases, `-c` rewrites,\nscripting). The gate exists to make accidental des"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"tructive calls fail loudly\nwith an explanation — deliberate destructive work is authorized through t"},{"id":"p15s4","text":"he\nconfigured policy, not by bypassing the gate."},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"**npm (recommended)** — from any directory:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"**From GitHub** (or a local checkout / tarball):"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Then restart `dsh --profile web`. For GitHub installs, pnpm asks you to\nallowlist the `prepare` buil"},{"id":"p21s2","text":"d script once (see the\nofficial packaging guide)."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"## Configuration"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"All options are optional; the defaults are shown below:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"- `deny` (default) — destructive calls are rejected with the pattern name and\nan explanation.\n- `ask"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"` — destructive calls go through the runtime's approval seam\n(`ctx.approval`); without a mounted app"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"roval service they degrade to `deny`.\n- `allow` — the gate passes everything through."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Development"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Prerequisites: Node.js ≥ 22.19 and pnpm. The project is self-contained — all\n`@deepseek-ai/*` types "},{"id":"p27s2","text":"resolve from the published public API (0.0.1-rc.5 line)\ninstalled as devDependencies, so no `deepsee"},{"id":"p27s3","text":"k-harness` checkout is required."},{"id":"p28s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The tests create a disposable repository, register the plugin on a Cordis\ncontext with the real `dsh"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"-tools` runtime, and execute every tool through the\nfull pipeline (`tools/pre-execute` → dispatch → "},{"id":"p29s3","text":" and execute every tool through the\nfull pipeline (`tools/pre-execute` → dispatch → `tools/result`)."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"## Publish"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"- `dsh.bundle.patch` in `package.json` points at `cordis.patch.yml`, so\n`dsh plugin add` activates t"},{"id":"p31s2","text":"he plugin as a profile layer.\n- `prepare` runs `tsdown --config tsdown.prepare.config.ts`, which tra"},{"id":"p31s3","text":"nspiles\n`src/` without project references — so GitHub installs build cleanly without\na sibling harne"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"ss checkout. Prefer publishing prebuilt tarballs / npm\npackages to avoid pnpm's build-script allowli"},{"id":"p31s5","text":"checkout. Prefer publishing prebuilt tarballs / npm\npackages to avoid pnpm's build-script allowlist."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"## License"},{"id":"p33s1","text":"MIT"}],"truncated":false}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
